#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:11
msgid "// No trait bounds on the type definition.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:14
msgid "// Instead bounds are put on the implementations for the type.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:18
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:29
msgid "\"{}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:21
msgid "// alternatively\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:24
msgid "// Specifies the trait bound in a where expression\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:36
msgid ""
"When authoring a type with generic parameters, we can write implementations "
"for that type that depend on what the parameters are or what traits they "
"implement."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:40
msgid "These methods are only available when the type meets those conditions."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:42
msgid ""
"For things like ordered sets, where you'd want the inner type to always be "
"`Ord`, this is the preferred way of putting a trait bound on a parameter of "
"a type."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:46
msgid ""
"We don't put the definition on the type itself as this would cause "
"downstream issues for everywhere the type is mentioned with a generic "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/conditional-methods.md:49
msgid ""
"We can maintain invariants just fine with conditional method implementations."
msgstr ""
